# Pinned SHA-256 digest of the committed baseline release artifact.
#
# The upgrade replay boots this exact bytecode and swaps the live instance
# over to the in-development build, so the bytes are the anchor for "what the
# released line wrote". The release workflow's attestation ceremony has not
# run yet (no v* tags exist), so this in-repo digest is what makes the
# artifact reproducible instead of trusted by assertion: every reader in
# `storage_golden` verifies the file against this line before using it, and
# `scripts/storage_golden_smoke.sh` checks it before any testnet deploy.
#
# Reproduce: build the v0.3.0 release-line source with
# `stellar contract build` (stellar-cli 28.1.0, rust-toolchain.toml channel),
# then `sha256sum target/wasm32v1-none/release/streampay_contract.wasm` must
# equal the line below. When release.yml first attests this build, its
# published SHA256SUMS entry must equal this digest; § "Replacing the
# baseline wasm" in docs/STORAGE_LAYOUT.md covers a legitimate change.
fa1b4481671bc1b9f65e52b3e97717aba072a666d0e32ed9cc493acaba10a11d  streampay-v0.3.0-baseline.wasm
